.TH "cbor::iov_writer" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::iov_writer \- A target of \fBcbor::encoder\fP that collects pieces, not one buffer\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/encode\&.hpp>\fP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
A target of \fBcbor::encoder\fP that collects pieces, not one buffer\&. 

The encoder writes heads and short strings into blocks of CBOR_ENCODER_BLOCK_SIZE bytes\&. A text or a byte string of 32 bytes or more that the program hands over with its owner becomes a piece of its own, with no copy\&. \fBcbor::encoder::finish()\fP gives the pieces as \fRstruct iovec\fP, in a \fR\fBref\fP\fP that holds the blocks and the owners\&. The pieces are for sending only, as \fBcbor::encode_iov()\fP says\&. The class exists where \fR<sys/uio\&.h>\fP exists\&. The class has no public member function\&. A write after \fRfinish\fP throws \fRstd::logic_error\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
call: cbor::iov_writer w; cbor::encoder e(w);
call: e\&.text_string(text), with text a std::shared_ptr<std::string const> of 40 times "x"
call: auto const pieces = e\&.finish()
(*pieces)\->size(): 2, the head 78 28 and *text with no copy
sent with writev: "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
    // text: a std::shared_ptr<std::string const> with 40 times "x"
    cbor::iov_writer w;
    cbor::encoder e(w);
    bool const written = e\&.text_string(text)\&.has_value();
    auto const pieces = e\&.finish();  // 2 pieces: the head 78 28, then *text with no copy
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::encode_iov()\fP 

.PP
\fBcbor::encoder\fP 
.RE
.PP

